<title>FRANCE: ONIC sees 6.4 pct rise in spring barley sowings.</title>
<headline>ONIC sees 6.4 pct rise in spring barley sowings.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French grain office ONIC said on Wednesday that sowings of spring barley for the 1997 harvest may rise by 6.4 percent to 481,000 hectares from 452,000 hectares.</p>
<p>The prediction released ahead of ONIC's monthly news conference was the first estimate this year for spring barley provided by ONIC.  </p>
<p>ONIC also said that maize sowings should remain stable at around 1.7 million hectares, in line with the previous estimates from the French maize growers' association.</p>
<p>ONIC also predicted that rapeseed sowings may rise 8.2 percent to around 947,000 hectares.</p>
</text>
